# Agentic BO

A working implementation of **agentic Bayesian optimization** as described in

> Brunzema, Tiao, Le, De Angeli, Xuan, Gligorijevic. *Agentic Bayesian Optimization through
> Surrogate-Augmented Autoresearch.* arXiv:2608.00316.

In agentic BO, an LLM agent is the decision maker of the optimization loop. At every
step it decides which probes, reconfigurations and proposals to run and which point to
evaluate next. A Bayesian backend supplies the surrogate models and acquisition
functions; the agent consults it, but the backend does not decide for it. The system
has two halves, and so does this package:

| Paper | Here | Role |
|---|---|---|
| **Sara** (LLM agent) | `agentic_bo.sara` | The metalevel policy: Claude through the Anthropic API, a deterministic scripted agent, and the classical baselines, all acting through the same tool interface. |
| **lenz** (BoTorch backend with a JSON CLI) | `agentic_bo.lenz` | GP surrogates, acquisition functions, a trial log and a command interface that the agent can inspect and reconfigure. Pure numpy/scipy. |

The core task is to optimize a black-box `f: X -> R` sequentially with a budget of `T`
evaluations, minimizing either **simple regret** `f* - max_t f(x_t)` or **cumulative
regret** `sum_t (f* - f(x_t))`.

